  "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation to isolate $\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x+\\sqrt{18} & =3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}\u2061x & =3\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{18} \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}\u2061x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can't find an equivalent equation involving tangent, since this would lead to us dividing by $0:$\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{0}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can instead find an equivalent equation using the fact that $\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}=0\n$$\n\nIn this case, we can find the principal solution as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x & =0 \\\\ x & =\\operatorname{arccos}\u20610 \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={90}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={90}^{\u2218}.$\n\nTo find more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{\u2218}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =x+{180}^{\u2218}={90}^{\u2218}+{180}^{\u2218}={270}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, our solutions are $x={90}^{\u2218}$ and $x={270}^{\u2218}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
